    body: "# Who everyone is\n\nThe map of the people around you — who they are, what they own, and enough of the human\nstuff that the team chat makes sense in week one.\n\n> **You are not expected to memorize this.** It's a lookup. Skim it once now so the names\n> aren't cold, then come back when someone appears in a thread and you can't place them.\n>\n> For **who to ask about what**, see [`how-the-ramp-works.md`](./how-the-ramp-works.md) —\n> that table is the practical version and it isn't repeated here.\n\n---\n\n## The picture\n\n```\n                                   Vineet Nargolwala\n                                   President & CEO\n                                          │\n                                   Olivier Bojarski\n                                   President, Americas & Asia\n                                          │\n                                   Stephen Sundstrom\n                                   VP & GM, Americas Marketing\n                                          │\n   ┌───────────────────┬──────────────────┴─┬─────────────────────┐\n   │                   │                    │                     │\n   Tyler Whitten       Julie Molsky         STUART MacKAY         Michele DiStasio\n   Marketing           Sr. Ecommerce        Sr. Digital           Channel Marketing\n   Analytics           Merchandising        Marketing             Director\n                                            ↑ your skip-level\n                                            │\n   ┌──────────────────┬──────────────────┬──┴───────────┐\n   │                  │                  │              │\n   Phil Martinez      Travis Harvey      Wendy Meyer    ALEX LANGTON\n   SEO Manager        Email Marketing    Email          Paid Media Manager\n   (+ Ben Youngblade, Specialist         Marketing      ★ your manager\n    Matt Bougie)                         Specialist\n```\n\n**Your team, zoomed in:**\n\n```\n            ALEX LANGTON — Paid Media Manager\n                            │\n   ┌──────────────┬─────────┴────┬────────────────┐\n   │              │              │                │\n   Courtney       Scott          CJ               ★ YOU\n   Hamilton       Palmersheim    Weissenberger    Paid Search\n   Sr. Paid       Paid Search    Paid Search      Associate\n   Search Spec.   Specialist     Specialist\n```\n\n**Where you sit:** four levels below the CEO, on a team of five including Alex. Most of\nAmericas Marketing sits in **Good Hope** (you'll see it written **GHO**). Stephen Sundstrom\nis in Camden, Michele DiStasio in Branford.\n\n> **A naming oddity worth knowing on day one:** Alex's team is formally called\n> **\"Digital Paid Media: Seton, Emedco\"** in Workday — even though it also runs Brady's paid\n> media and PDC's. The name is a leftover, not a scope statement. Don't read anything into it.\n\n---\n\n## Your team\n\n### Alex Langton — Paid Media Manager · your manager\n\nOwns paid media across the Americas — Brady, Seton, EMEDCO, PDC, Mecco, Amazon. Your 1:1 is\n**analyst-led**, meaning you bring the agenda, and he doesn't push work through a ticket\ntracker. **Practical consequence: Google Chat is the expected way to get unblocked, not a\nlast resort.** If you're stuck at 10am, message him at 10am.\n\nHe builds systems rather than one-off documents — this repo is an example — and he'll ask\nyou to leave something behind at the end of most projects for the same reason.\n\n### Courtney Hamilton — Senior Paid Search Specialist · your peer buddy\n\nMoving toward a **strategist** role: Brady Mexico, Canada and Brazil, plus social\n(LinkedIn, Facebook, Reddit) and trade publications. She led the Apple Ads launch. She's the\nperson to ask \"is this normal?\" without it costing you anything.\n\n**On her register:** ALL-CAPS enthusiasm, \"im dead / im obsessed,\" countdowns to margarita\nhour, and she will start an office scavenger hunt unprompted. There's a long-running bit\nabout her eyesight — she once couldn't identify something at 12× zoom and the team has never\nlet it go. Dogs **Goose** and **Blu** (she wanted \"Bleu\"; her husband vetoed the spelling).\nShe would like a dog-friendly office more than she'd like most things.\n\n> ⚠️ **Sharp sarcasm is her default setting, not a signal.** New people occasionally read\n> friction into it. There isn't any.\n\n### Scott Palmersheim — Paid Search Specialist\n\nCurrently on **PDC Healthcare and Wristbands** — the accounts moving to you — and heading\ntoward **Seton US, EMEDCO and Seton Canada**. He also owns the trade-publication budget and\nhas built a set of his own automation tools on Google's AI stack.\n\n**On his register:** the quiet one, until a very well-timed dry one-liner lands. The room's\nrunning joke is that Scott is the team's child, complete with periodic child-labor-law\ncommentary. He plays along.\n\n### CJ Weissenberger — Paid Search Specialist\n\nCurrently **Seton US, EMEDCO and Seton Canada**, plus **Amazon** day to day, and moving over\nto the **Brady** accounts — which he's openly delighted about (`#TeamBrady`). He ran the\nSeton/EMEDCO family before the current shuffle, so the most recent hands-on knowledge of\nthose accounts is his. He's also a genuinely good forecaster and relentlessly\nself-deprecating about it.\n\n**On his register:** his own words — *\"Snarky, passive aggressive sarcasm is my specialty.\"*\nReacts in GIFs first and words second. Calls Alex \"Mr Bossman.\"\n\n> ⚠️ **His first name is Conrad.** That's where the \"CJ\" comes from, and it's the kind of\n> thing you only find out by emailing the wrong address once.\n\n---\n\n## The rest of Stuart's team\n\nStuart's \"Digital Marketing\" group is **three functions, not one**: SEO, Email and Paid\nMedia. You'll see all three in the same threads.\n\n### Phil Martinez — SEO Manager\n\nRuns SEO for Brady and Healthcare, and does a lot of the execution himself. **Paid and\norganic compete for the same search terms**, so he's worth knowing before you build out\nnegatives, not after.\n\n**On his register:** low frequency, high quality. Dry. He was also the target of a\nduck-based office prank substantial enough that it's still referenced months later, and\nStuart's defense of him during it is remembered as a small classic.\n\n### Ben Youngblade — Senior SEO Analyst\n\nUnder Phil. Recently moved from **PDC to Seton/EMEDCO/Canada** on the SEO side — which means\n**he has made almost exactly the transition you're making, across exactly your two account\ngroups.** He has no stake in your paid-search work, so he can be completely candid. An early\nconversation with him is one of the highest-value hours available to you.\n\n**On his register:** a dad-joke-of-the-week ritual, wholehearted enthusiasm about\nconference swag, and the author of an extended saga concerning fridge etiquette and justice\nthat escalated well beyond its subject matter.\n\n### Matt Bougie — SEO / content\n\nAlso under Phil. The measured devil's advocate — during the fridge saga he re-ran the actual\nmath on it, which tells you most of what you need to know about how he engages with things.\n\n### Travis Harvey (\"TJ\") — Email Marketing Specialist\n\nEmail. **On his register:** the GIF-and-zinger guy. Alex rates his one-liners highly, which\nis not a thing he says about many people.\n\n### Wendy Meyer — Email Marketing Specialist\n\nEmail. **We don't have a note on Wendy beyond the role** — which is a gap in this file, not\na comment on her. Introduce yourself early and fix it.\n\n---\n\n## Up the chain\n\n### Stuart MacKay — Sr. Digital Marketing Manager · your skip-level\n\nAlex's manager. Your work has to eventually show up in numbers Stuart cares about: revenue,\nnon-brand quality traffic, efficiency inside guardrails, and **the reason a number moved**.\n\nThe one line of his worth internalizing early:\n\n> *\"You either get the opportunity to make a recommendation or you'll get terms dictated to\n> you.\"*\n\nThat's the whole reason your Day-90 target is \"brings recommendations, not open questions.\"\nHe runs **GSD** meetings — Get Shit Done: pick a topic, debate it properly, agree the next\nstep, then everyone commits including whoever lost the argument.\n\n**On his register:** **\"Stu(pid) fact of the week\"**, a Friday ritual in the team chat, past\nentries including how pigeons navigate by liver and the size of Australia's largest recorded\ncockroach seizure. His signature move is the one-word reply — a fully-formed question met\nwith *\"no\"*. Roasting runs both directions between him and the whole paid team, and he\ndefends their actual work fiercely inside the same breath as the joke.\n\n### Stephen Sundstrom — VP & General Manager, Americas Marketing\n\nTwo levels above you, in Camden. Stuart's manager. Four functions report to him: Analytics,\nEcommerce Merchandising, Digital Marketing and Channel Marketing.\n\n### Olivier Bojarski — President, Americas & Asia · and Vineet Nargolwala — President & CEO\n\nBig budget approvals route up through Olivier. Vineet is the CEO — the all-hands\nis called **\"AskV\"**, which is where the V comes from. You will not need either of them, but\nyou'll hear both names.\n\n---\n\n## The teams you'll actually deal with\n\n| Team | Who | What you'll need them for |\n|------|-----|--------------------------|\n| **Marketing Analytics** | **Tyler Whitten** (manager), Jared Sarabia, Alexandra Schroeder | BigQuery, attribution, Power BI. Getting your BigQuery access sorted is an early task |\n| **Ecommerce Merchandising** | Julie Molsky → Adam Lockwood → **Matt Kashuda** | The bradyid.com site tools. Matt K is Alex's near-daily partner on the finder widgets |\n| **Marketing Operations** | **Matthew Ryno** (\"Matt R\") | Salesforce lead routing. He is a one-person show being pulled in every direction — **come with a specific ask**, not an open-ended one, and you'll both have a better day |\n| **Creative Services** | Ryan Calverley (director), **Jim Sharp** (HPS brand & creative), Courtney Culp and Ben Wischnewski (copy) | Brand and creative assets. Jim Sharp is your PDC contact |\n| **SEO** | Phil Martinez, Ben Youngblade, Matt Bougie | Before you build negatives — see above |\n| **Finance** | Brittiany | Forecasts and budget. Mostly reaches you through Alex |\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ The name traps\n\nThis is the section you'll actually come back to. **When a first name is ambiguous in a\nthread, just ask which one** — everybody does it.\n\n| The name | Who they might be |\n|----------|-------------------|\n| **Alex** | **Alex Langton** (your manager) · **Alexandra Schroeder** (Sr. Marketing Web Analyst, Tyler's team) · **Alex Krause** (Marketing) |\n| **Matt** | **Matt Kashuda** (\"Matt K\") — ecommerce, the site tools · **Matthew Ryno** (\"Matt R\") — MOps and Salesforce routing · **Matt Bougie** — SEO/content |\n| **Courtney** | **Courtney Hamilton** — your teammate · **Courtney Culp** — Sr. Copywriter in Creative Services |\n| **CJ** | **CJ Weissenberger** — your teammate · **CJ Noggle** — ran paid search years ago, appears only in old budget files |\n| **Michele / Michelle** | **Michele DiStasio** (Channel Marketing Director) · **Michele Kowalkowski** (Digital Merchandising Ops) · a third **Michelle** on ABM, who is departing |\n| **Ben** | **Ben Youngblade** — SEO, the one you want · **Ben Wischnewski** — Sr. Copywriter, Creative Services |\n| **Tyler** | **Tyler Whitten** — Marketing Analytics Manager · Courtney's husband is also a Tyler, which comes up more often than you'd think |\n\n> ⚠️ And the biggest one, which isn't a person: **\"Brady\" is the company, the flagship brand\n> *and* a former NFL quarterback.** More on why that third one costs money in\n> [`who-else-is-searching.md`](../02-learning/who-else-is-searching.md).\n\n---\n\n## One note on the jokes\n\nThe team chat is a running roast and it will look impenetrable for a few weeks. Two things\nworth knowing:\n\n1. **You don't have to be funny to belong here.** Nobody is scoring your contributions.\n2. **The roasting and the work are separate.** People who spend the morning trading insults\n   will defend each other's work without hesitation in the next meeting. If the register\n   ever reads as hostile, it isn't — and Alex or Courtney will tell you the same thing if\n   you ask.\n\nIf something in this file turns out to be wrong or out of date, fix it. You'll meet these\npeople with fresh eyes, which is the one time anybody notices."
